[1m[38;5;10mstbds_siphash_bytes[0m in [38;5;10msrc/lib.rs[0m[22m — The main loop and tail case 4 had an integer promotion mismatch with C:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- **C behavior**: [38;5;10md[0] | (d[1] << 8) | (d[2] << 16) | (d[3] << 24)[0m is computed in [38;5;10mint[0m arithmetic. When [38;5;10md[3] >= 128[0m, the [38;5;10m<< 24[0m produces a negative [38;5;10mint[0m, which sign-extends when assigned to [38;5;10msize_t[0m.[0m[0m
- **Rust (before fix)**: Used [38;5;10mas usize[0m throughout, which zero-extends — no sign extension, producing different hashes for any data containing bytes ≥ 128 at positions where [38;5;10md[3][0m or [38;5;10md[7][0m are read.[0m[0m
- **Fix**: Changed to compute the 4-byte groups as [38;5;10mi32[0m first (matching C's [38;5;10mint[0m), then cast to [38;5;10musize[0m to get the same sign-extension behavior.[0m[0m
